  <main>

    <div class="container">
      <div class="page-header">

        <div class="kicker">
          Research
        </div>

        <h1>
          Traditional<br>
          music in<br>
          transition
        </h1>

        <div class="page-intro">
          I study how traditional music moves between communities,
          independent cultural scenes, institutions and global music
          infrastructures — and how these movements are shaped by
          colonial and capitalist hierarchies.
        </div>

      </div>
    </div>


    <section>
      <div class="container section-grid">

        <h2 class="section-title">
          Current Research
        </h2>

        <div class="content">

          <p class="large-text">
            My current research focuses on new trajectories of traditional
            music and on non-academic methods of working with musical
            traditions.
          </p>

          <p>
            I am interested in what happens when traditional music moves
            beyond the contexts in which it has conventionally been
            documented, represented and performed, and enters independent
            labels, festivals, clubs, media, artistic institutions and
            contemporary music scenes.
          </p>

          <p>
            The project examines the people and infrastructures surrounding
            this music: musicians, independent labels, curators, festivals,
            venues, journalists, researchers and audiences.
          </p>

          <p>
            Rather than approaching traditional music exclusively as
            heritage or preservation, I am interested in it as a living
            cultural practice that participates in contemporary processes
            of identity formation, migration, political imagination and
            cultural production.
          </p>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section>
      <div class="container section-grid">

        <h2 class="section-title">
          Questions
        </h2>

        <div class="content">

          <div class="research-list">

            <div class="research-item">
              <div class="research-label">
                Circulation
              </div>

              <div class="research-text">
                How does traditional music enter contemporary European
                and global music markets, festivals, media and cultural
                institutions?
              </div>
            </div>


            <div class="research-item">
              <div class="research-label">
                Mediation
              </div>

              <div class="research-text">
                What roles do labels, curators, journalists, festivals
                and other intermediaries play in determining how
                traditional music is heard and understood?
              </div>
            </div>


            <div class="research-item">
              <div class="research-label">
                Decoloniality
              </div>

              <div class="research-text">
                How are colonial hierarchies reproduced or challenged
                through categories such as folk, world music,
                authenticity, tradition and contemporary music?
              </div>
            </div>


            <div class="research-item">
              <div class="research-label">
                Identity
              </div>

              <div class="research-text">
                How can traditional music contribute to the formation
                and preservation of identity and to horizontal
                connections between communities?
              </div>
            </div>


            <div class="research-item">
              <div class="research-label">
                Knowledge
              </div>

              <div class="research-text">
                What forms of knowledge are produced outside academia
                by musicians, labels, archives, communities, journalists
                and independent cultural practitioners?
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section>
      <div class="container section-grid">

        <h2 class="section-title">
          Göttingen
        </h2>

        <div class="content">

          <div class="institution">

            <h3>
              Institute of Cultural Anthropology / European Ethnology
            </h3>

            <p>
              I am currently a Guest Researcher at the Institute of
              Cultural Anthropology / European Ethnology (KAEE) at the
              University of Göttingen.
            </p>

            <p>
              My research in Göttingen is supported by the
              Right Livelihood Foundation.
            </p>

            <p>
              The project draws on interviews with musicians, curators,
              label founders, journalists and cultural practitioners,
              alongside academic and journalistic literature, artistic
              works, archival materials and my own experience of working
              with traditional and independent music.
            </p>

          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>


    <section>
      <div class="container section-grid">

        <h2 class="section-title">
          Background
        </h2>

        <div class="content">

          <p>
            My academic research grows out of more than a decade of
            practical work with traditional music through Ored Recordings
            and related cultural projects.
          </p>

          <p>
            This position — between research, journalism, music production,
            curatorial work and independent cultural practice — is central
            to my approach.
          </p>

          <p>
            Over the years, I have participated in activities at SOAS
            University of London, the University of Vienna, the Higher
            School of Economics, Ilia State University and the Philharmonic
            Society of Rouen as a visiting researcher, invited speaker
            or collaborator.
          </p>

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

